.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
We provide various algorithms to invert the communication pattern\&. 

The task at hand is: given an individual set of receiver ranks for each process in a sender role, compute efficiently for the receiver role of each rank the set of senders to it\&.
.PP
This file implements two approaches that solve the problem scalably\&.
.PP
.IP "1." 4
The first and original historic one offers the choice between a binary tree recursion, an n-ary tree recursion, optionally with payload data, and an allgather version\&. The n-ary tree version contains the binary one as a special case\&. It is called \fBsc_notify_nary\fP and can be configured by the global variables
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fBsc_notify_nary_ntop_default\fP; #children of the root tree node,
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fBsc_notify_nary_nint_default\fP; #children of intermediate nodes,
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fBsc_notify_nary_nbot_default\fP; #siblings of each leaf node\&.
.PP
.PP
Thus it can be tailored to match for example distributed NUMA architectures\&. The default for each variable is a conservative 2 to choose a binary tree\&.
.PP
Another addition to the family is \fBsc_notify_ext\fP for the best known default, which is currently the PEX algorithm\&.
.IP "2." 4
The more recent and general variant allows to choose between practically all currently known algorithms, enumerated by \fBsc_notify_type_t\fP\&. This is managed by first creating a configuration object \fBsc_notify_t\fP, setting its type and further parameters, and passing it into the general \fBsc_notify_payload\fP or \fBsc_notify_payloadv\fP functions\&. 
.PP

.SH "Enumeration Type Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "enum \fBsc_notify_type_t\fP"

.PP
Various equivalent implementations of the functionality\&. 
.PP
\fBEnumerator\fP
.in +1c
.TP
\fB\fISC_NOTIFY_DEFAULT \fP\fP
Choose whatever type is stored in sc_notify_type_default\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISC_NOTIFY_ALLGATHER \fP\fP
Choose allgather algorithm\&. Likely suboptimal\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISC_NOTIFY_BINARY \fP\fP
Choose simple binary recursion\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISC_NOTIFY_NARY \fP\fP
Choose nary (k-way) recursion\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISC_NOTIFY_PEX \fP\fP
Choose alltoall algorithm (AKA personalized exchange)\&. Current best choice\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISC_NOTIFY_PCX \fP\fP
Choose reduce_scatter algorithm (AKA personalized census)\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISC_NOTIFY_RSX \fP\fP
Choose remote summation algorithm\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISC_NOTIFY_NBX \fP\fP
Choose non-blocking consensus algorithm\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISC_NOTIFY_RANGES \fP\fP
Use the sc_ranges functionality\&. Likely suboptimal\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISC_NOTIFY_SUPERSET \fP\fP
Use a computable superset of communicators, computed by a callback function\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISC_NOTIFY_NUM_TYPES \fP\fP
End of list marker for notify algorithms\&. 
.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "int sc_notify (int * receivers, int num_receivers, int * senders, int * num_senders, \fBsc_MPI_Comm\fP mpicomm)"

.PP
Collective call to notify a set of receiver ranks of current rank\&. More generally, this function serves to transpose the nonzero pattern of a matrix, where each row and column corresponds to an MPI rank in order\&. We use a binary tree to construct the communication pattern\&. This minimizes the number of messages at the cost of more messages compared to a fatter tree such as configurable with \fBsc_notify_nary\fP\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIreceivers\fP Sorted and unique array of MPI ranks to inform\&. 
.br
\fInum_receivers\fP Count of ranks contained in receivers\&. 
.br
\fIsenders\fP Array of at least size sc_MPI_Comm_size\&. On output it contains the notifying ranks, whose number is returned in \fBnum_senders\fP\&. 
.br
\fInum_senders\fP On output the number of notifying ranks\&. 
.br
\fImpicomm\fP MPI communicator to use\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Aborts on MPI error or returns sc_MPI_SUCCESS\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int sc_notify_allgather (int * receivers, int num_receivers, int * senders, int * num_senders, \fBsc_MPI_Comm\fP mpicomm)"

.PP
Collective call to notify a set of receiver ranks of current rank\&. This version uses one call to sc_MPI_Allgather and one to sc_MPI_Allgatherv\&. We provide hand-coded alternatives \fBsc_notify\fP and \fBsc_notify_nary\fP\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIreceivers\fP Sorted and unique array of MPI ranks to inform\&. 
.br
\fInum_receivers\fP Count of ranks contained in receivers\&. 
.br
\fIsenders\fP Array of at least size sc_MPI_Comm_size\&. On output it contains the notifying ranks\&. 
.br
\fInum_senders\fP On output the number of notifying ranks\&. 
.br
\fImpicomm\fP MPI communicator to use\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Aborts on MPI error or returns sc_MPI_SUCCESS\&. 
.RE
.PP

