.SS "void sc_notify_payload (\fBsc_array_t\fP * receivers, \fBsc_array_t\fP * senders, \fBsc_array_t\fP * in_payload, \fBsc_array_t\fP * out_payload, int sorted, \fBsc_notify_t\fP * notify)"

.PP
Collective call to notify a set of receiver ranks of current rank\&. This function aborts on MPI error\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIreceivers\fP On input, sorted and uniqued array of type int\&. Contains the MPI ranks to inform\&. If \fBsenders\fP is not NULL, treated read-only\&. If \fBsenders\fP is NULL, takes its role on output\&. In this case it must not be a view\&. 
.br
\fIsenders\fP If NULL, the result is placed in \fBreceivers\fP as written below for the non-NULL case\&. If not NULL, array of type int and any length\&. Its entries on input are ignored and overwritten\&. On output it is resized to the number of notifying ranks, which it contains in order\&. Thus, it must not be a view\&. 
.br
\fIin_payload\fP This array pointer may be NULL\&. If not NULL, it must have \fBnum_receivers\fP entries that are the same size on every process\&. If not NULL and \fBout_payload\fP is NULL, it must not be a view, and it will be resized to contain the output and have \fB*num_senders\fP entries\&. 
.br
\fIout_payload\fP This array pointer may be NULL\&. If not, it must not be a view, and on output will have \fB*\fP num_senders entries\&. 
.br
\fIsorted\fP whether \fBreceivers\fP and \fBsenders\fP are required to be sorted by MPI rank\&. 
.br
\fInotify\fP Notify controller to use\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void sc_notify_payloadv (\fBsc_array_t\fP * receivers, \fBsc_array_t\fP * senders, \fBsc_array_t\fP * out_payload, \fBsc_array_t\fP * in_payload, \fBsc_array_t\fP * out_offsets, \fBsc_array_t\fP * in_offsets, int sorted, \fBsc_notify_t\fP * notify)"

.PP
Collective call to notify a set of receiver ranks of current rank and send a variable size message to the receiver\&. This function aborts on MPI error\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIreceivers\fP On input, sorted and uniqued array of type int\&. Contains the MPI ranks to inform\&. If \fBsenders\fP is not NULL, treated read-only\&. If \fBsenders\fP is NULL, takes its role on output\&. In this case it must not be a view\&. 
.br
\fIsenders\fP If NULL, the result is placed in \fBreceivers\fP as written below for the non-NULL case\&. If not NULL, array of type int and any length\&. Its entries on input are ignored and overwritten\&. On output it is resized to the number of notifying ranks, which it contains in order\&. Thus, it must not be a view\&. 
.br
\fIin_payload\fP This array pointer may be NULL\&. If not, it must not be a view and have entries that are the same size on every process\&. This data will be communicated to the receivers\&. If \fBout_payload\fP is NULL, this will be resized to contain the received payload\&. 
.br
\fIout_payload\fP This array pointer may be NULL\&. If not, it must not be a view and have entries that are the same size on every process\&. If not NULL, this array will be resized to contain the received payload\&. 
.br
\fIin_offsets\fP If \fBin_payload\fP is not NULL, this is an array of int's of size \fBnum_receivers\fP + 1, giving offsets for the portion of the payload to be sent to every receiver\&. If \fBout_offsets\fP is NULL, it will be resized to give offsets of the received payload\&. 
.br
\fIout_offsets\fP This array pointer may be NULL\&. If \fBin_payload\fP is not NULL, it is an array of int's that will be resized to \fBnum_senders\fP + 1, giving offsets for the portion of the payload received from each sender\&. 
.br
\fIsorted\fP whether \fBreceivers\fP and \fBsenders\fP (and thus \fBin_offsets\fP and \fBout_offsets\fP) are required to be sorted by MPI rank\&. 
.br
\fInotify\fP Notify controller to use\&. 
.RE
.PP

